* The Status endpoints are of particular interest and provide information on the derivative price, spot price, mark price, insurance fund balance, next funding timestamp, next funding accrued, next funding step, current funding, and open interest all from a single endpoint.

### Authenticated derivatives data

Instructions on how to use authenticated endpoints can be found here:

* [Rest Authentication](https://docs.bitfinex.com/docs/rest-auth)
* [WebSocket Authentication](https://docs.bitfinex.com/docs/ws-auth)

The following authenticated endpoints provide information relevant to trading derivatives:

<Table align={["left","left"]}>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>
        REST V2
      </th>

      <th>
        WS V2
      </th>
    </tr>
  </thead>

  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>
        Wallets info:  

        * [Wallets](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-wallets)  

        Active orders and positions:  

        * [Retrieve Orders](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-retrieve-orders)  
        * [Retrieve Positions](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-positions)  
        * [Positions Audit](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-positions-audit)  

        Reports:  

        * [Orders History](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/orders-history)  
        * [Order Trades](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-order-trades)  
        * [Trades](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-public-trades)  
        * [Ledgers](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ledgers) (\*USDt0)  
        * [Positions History](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-positions-history)
      </td>

      <td>
        Wallets info:  

        * [Wallets](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-wallets)  

        Active orders and positions:  

        * [Orders](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-orders)  
        * [Positions](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-positions)  

        Reports:  

        * [Historical Orders (deprecated)](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-historical-orders)  
        * [Trades](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-trades)
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</Table>

### Converting funds

Derivatives trading requires USDt0 in your derivatives wallet. Conversion and transfer can be done on the website following these instructions:

* [Knowledge Base: How to convert USDt to USDt0](https://support.bitfinex.com/hc/en-us/articles/360035475154-How-to-convert-USDt-to-USDt0)

Alternatively, the API allows conversion through the following endpoint:

* [Transfer Between Wallets](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-transfer)

### Trading derivatives through the API

You can submit, update, and cancel your derivative trades using the following endpoints:

> 📘 Trading pairs
>
> To use these endpoints for derivative trading, specify the trading pair as either tBTCF0:USTF0 or ETHF0:USTF0

<Table align={["left","left"]}>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>
        REST V2
      </th>

      <th>
        WS V2

        \*
      </th>
    </tr>
  </thead>

  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>
        * [Submit Order](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-submit-order)  
        * [Order Update](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-update-order)  
        * [Order Multi-OP](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-order-multi)  
        * [Cancel Order Multi](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-order-cancel-multi)  
        * [Derivative Position Collateral](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/rest-auth-deriv-pos-collateral-set)
      </td>

      <td>
        * [New Order](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input-order-new)  
        * [Update Order](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input-order-update)  
        * [Order Multi-OP](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input-order-multi-op)  
        * [Cancel Order](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input-order-cancel)  
        * [Cancel Order Multi](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input-order-cancel-multi)
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</Table>

* See [Input API](https://docs.bitfinex.com/reference/ws-auth-input) for details on placing, updating, and canceling orders through WS.